-- title:
--   Construction of an entropy pair for every rank and budget
-- statement:
--   These notions belong to a counterexample to the duality conjecture for metric entropy. For every $a,b\ge1$ there are $n$ and a symmetric convex body $K\subset\mathbb R^n$ with $\log N(K,Q_n)>b\log N(Q_n^\circ,a^{-1}K^\circ)$. Here $Q_n=[-1,1]^n$ is the cube, $K^\circ=\{y:\langle x,y\rangle\le1\text{ for all }x\in K\}$ is the polar (so $Q_n^\circ$ is the $\ell_1$ ball), and $N(A,B)$ is the least number of translates of $B$ covering $A$. Let $\beta(a,r,B)=\dfrac{2R^2s}{r+R-1}+\dfrac2B$, where $R=h(a)$ is the compression radius and $s=\lceil1000a\rceil$ the number of pivot slots. For every $a\ge1$, $r\ge1$ and $B>0$, there is an entropy pair for $(a,r,B)$: a symmetric convex body $K\subset\mathbb R^n$ with $n\ge r$, finite covers, $N(K,Q_n)>1$ and
--   $$
--   0\le\frac{\log N(Q_n^\circ,a^{-1}K^\circ)}{\log N(K,Q_n)}<\beta(a,r,B) .
--   $$
--
--   The construction takes only the numerical inputs; the prime, directions, matrix and body are all built from them.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Analysis/MetricEntropy/Construction.lean#L21-L98

